This notbook takess our non-aggregated shot-level data and aggregates it for use with aggregated binomial models

```{r}
nonagg_data <- read_parquet(here(clean_data_dir, "shot_level_defender_matchup_data.parquet"))
```

```{r}
aggregated_data <- nonagg_data |> 
  select(game_date:shot_type, defense_distance_category, defender_position, defender_foul_count) |> 
  group_by(game_id, slug_team_off, slug_team_def, primary_defender, shot_action, shot_zone, shot_area, shot_distance_ft, shot_type, defender_position, defender_foul_count) |> 
  summarize(shots_defended_made = sum(shot_made),
         shots_defended_total = n())
```

There are 21 games in which players play with more than 5 fouls. Spot checking the true number of personal fouls of each of these games, this seems to be a data quality issue having to do with action descriptions. For the purposes of this analysis, we'll drop these games from our sample. 
